📊 Statistical Analysis of Instagram Engagement for Sugar Cosmetics Using Python
Business Problem
Sugar Cosmetics publishes 50,000+ Instagram posts across multiple campaign types, content formats, audience segments, and hashtag strategies. However, the marketing team lacked statistical evidence to determine which content strategies genuinely improve engagement. Relying solely on descriptive metrics could lead to ineffective content planning, inefficient marketing spend, and missed opportunities for audience growth.
This project applies inferential statistics to validate marketing assumptions and identify the factors that significantly influence Instagram engagement.
________________________________________
Business Objectives
This project was designed to answer the following business questions:
•	Do different content types generate significantly different engagement? 
•	Which campaign strategies lead to higher audience interaction? 
•	Does audience emotion affect post performance? 
•	Does engagement source influence visibility? 
•	Does hashtag usage significantly impact engagement? 
•	Does posting day, month, or quarter influence performance? 
•	Are weekday and weekend posts statistically different? 
•	Which marketing variables should be prioritized to maximize engagement? 
________________________________________
Project Description
Performed an end-to-end statistical analysis on 50,000 Instagram posts using Python to evaluate the impact of 5 primary marketing variables (Post Type, Campaign Type, Audience Emotion, Engagement Source, and Hashtag Count) across 9 engagement KPIs. Applied 20+ statistical hypothesis tests, including Kruskal–Wallis, Mann–Whitney U, Chi-Square, and Bonferroni post-hoc analysis, to identify statistically significant engagement drivers and convert descriptive social media metrics into evidence-based marketing recommendations.
________________________________________
