________________________________________
Key Business Findings
1. Engagement Rate Across Marketing Variables
Business Question
Which marketing variables significantly influence Instagram engagement rate?
Statistical Findings
The Kruskal–Wallis analysis evaluated engagement rates across:
•	Post Type 
•	Campaign Type 
•	Audience Emotion 
•	Engagement Source 
•	Hashtag Count 
Among all variables, Hashtag Count demonstrated a statistically significant impact on engagement rate.
Post-hoc Analysis
Bonferroni comparisons showed:
•	Category 1 vs Category 2: Adjusted p = 0.047 (Significant) 
•	Category 1 vs Category 3: p = 0.615 
•	Category 2 vs Category 3: p = 0.755 
Business Interpretation
The improvement in engagement rate was primarily driven by differences between Hashtag Count Categories 1 and 2, while additional hashtags beyond that level provided no statistically significant improvement.
Business Recommendation
Standardize optimal hashtag usage instead of maximizing hashtag quantity.
________________________________________
2. Campaign Strategy Performance
Business Question
Do different campaign strategies influence social media performance?
Statistical Results
Campaign type significantly affected:
•	Comments: H = 10.917, p = 0.028 
•	Saves: H = 7.837, p = 0.098 
No statistically significant differences were observed for:
•	Impressions 
•	Reach 
•	Likes 
•	Shares 
•	Profile Visits 
•	Follows 
Post-hoc Analysis
For Comments:
•	Campaign 1 vs Campaign 3: Adjusted p = 0.029 
No campaign pairs remained significant for Saves after Bonferroni correction.
Business Interpretation
Campaign strategies primarily influenced deeper audience interactions (Comments and Saves) rather than visibility metrics.
Business Recommendation
Replicate campaign structures similar to Campaign 3, which generated significantly stronger audience conversations.
________________________________________
3. Audience Emotion
Business Question
Does audience emotion significantly affect engagement?
Statistical Results
Across all 9 engagement metrics, no statistically significant differences were identified.
Business Interpretation
Audience emotion alone does not appear to influence Instagram performance within this dataset.
Business Recommendation
Prioritize content quality and campaign execution over emotion-based content segmentation.
________________________________________
4. Engagement Source
Business Question
Does engagement source affect content visibility?
Statistical Results
Significant differences were observed for:
•	Impressions: H = 8.611, p = 0.035 
•	Reach: H = 6.660, p = 0.084 
No significant differences existed for:
•	Likes 
•	Comments 
•	Shares 
•	Saves 
•	Profile Visits 
•	Follows 
Post-hoc Analysis
Impressions:
•	Engagement Category 1 vs 4: Adjusted p = 0.042 
•	Hedges' g = 0.034 
Reach:
•	Engagement Category 1 vs 4: Adjusted p = 0.081 
•	Hedges' g = 0.031 
Business Interpretation
Although statistically significant, both comparisons exhibited very small practical effect sizes, suggesting limited real-world marketing impact.
Business Recommendation
Engagement source should be monitored but should not become the primary optimization strategy.
________________________________________
5. Hashtag Strategy
Business Question
How important is hashtag usage for engagement?
Statistical Results
Hashtag Count emerged as the only variable producing statistically significant differences in overall engagement rate.
The significant improvement occurred specifically between:
•	Category 1 and Category 2 (Adjusted p = 0.047) 
Business Interpretation
Moving from low to moderate hashtag usage improves engagement, while additional hashtags provide diminishing returns.
Business Recommendation
Develop standardized hashtag guidelines focused on optimal usage rather than maximum usage.
________________________________________
6. Temporal Analysis
Business Question
Does posting time influence Instagram performance?
Statistical Results
Performance was evaluated across:
•	Day of Week 
•	Month 
•	Quarter 
Across all 9 KPIs, no statistically significant differences were observed.
Business Interpretation
Posting schedule has minimal influence on Instagram performance.
Business Recommendation
Marketing teams should prioritize content quality instead of investing resources into identifying "perfect" posting times.
________________________________________
7. Weekday vs Weekend Performance
Business Question
Do weekday and weekend posts perform differently?
Engagement Rate
•	Mann–Whitney U = 253,472,766 
•	p = 0.569 
•	Rank-Biserial Correlation = 0.003 
No statistically significant difference was observed.
________________________________________
Other Performance Metrics
Statistically significant differences were detected for:
•	Impressions (p = 0.098) 
•	Reach (p = 0.080) 
•	Likes (p = 0.081) 
However,
•	Rank-Biserial Correlation ≈ 0.01 
indicated negligible practical impact.
Business Interpretation
Weekend posting offers little measurable advantage, despite isolated statistical significance.
Business Recommendation
Marketing teams should optimize content rather than shifting publishing schedules.
________________________________________
8. Content Distribution Bias
Business Question
Could scheduling bias explain engagement differences?
Statistical Results
Chi-Square tests demonstrated that:
•	Content characteristics remained consistently distributed across 
o	Months 
o	Quarters 
o	Weekdays 
Business Interpretation
Observed engagement differences are unlikely to be caused by scheduling bias.
Business Recommendation
This strengthens confidence that significant findings are driven by genuine content characteristics rather than uneven publishing behaviour.
________________________________________
Overall Business Impact
Using 20+ statistical hypothesis tests across 50,000 Instagram posts, this project transformed descriptive social media analytics into statistically validated marketing insights.
The analysis:
•	Evaluated 8 business variables across 9 engagement KPIs. 
•	Identified Hashtag Count as the strongest statistically significant driver of engagement, with meaningful improvement between low and moderate hashtag usage (Adjusted p = 0.047). 
•	Demonstrated that Campaign Strategy significantly influences audience interactions through Comments (H = 10.917, p = 0.028) and Saves (H = 7.837, p = 0.098). 
•	Confirmed that Posting Schedule (Day, Month, Quarter) has no significant impact on Instagram performance. 
•	Showed that Weekday vs Weekend posting produces only negligible practical effects (Rank-Biserial Correlation ≈ 0.01) despite isolated statistical differences. 
•	Eliminated Audience Emotion as a significant predictor of engagement across all performance metrics. 
•	Validated that engagement differences are driven by content strategy rather than scheduling bias, enabling evidence-based optimization of social media campaigns. 
________________________________________
Business Recommendations
•	Standardize optimal hashtag usage, as moderate hashtag counts significantly outperform lower usage while additional hashtags provide limited benefit. 
•	Prioritize campaign designs that encourage comments and saves, as these were the only audience interaction metrics significantly influenced by campaign strategy. 
•	Focus marketing optimization on content quality, creative execution, and hashtag strategy rather than posting schedules. 
•	Use engagement source insights as supplementary indicators, recognizing that statistically significant visibility differences exhibit minimal practical impact. 
•	Integrate hypothesis testing into future social media reporting to ensure campaign decisions are based on statistically validated evidence rather than descriptive metrics alone. 
